      "flagged": true,
      "answer": "Here is the answer to the question:\n\n**Objective:** Run a SELECT query against the site database from a custom module.\n\nTo run a SELECT query against the site database from a custom module, you can use the database service provided by Drupal. \n\nYou can inject the database service into your custom module like this: [code] public function getDatabase($connection) { $database = \\Drupal::database(); $query = $database->query(\"SELECT nid FROM {node}\"); return $query; } [/code]\n\nYou can also use the dependency injection container to inject the database service into your custom module. This is the recommended approach.\n\nVersion notes: This code is compatible with Drupal 10. \n\n[Please note that this answer is based on the provided evidence and does not include any external knowledge or assumptions.]",
